Observation (not a failure)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Listed createdAt uses directory birthtime. On this disk the three updtest
instance directories share an inode birth of 2026-10-30 18:11:26 +0100, while
ctime and docker CreatedAt show the 2026-11-10 23:21 install. Catch-up therefore
wrote 2026-10-30 .. 2026-11-10 rather than only 2026-11-10. The existence check
itself is correct against the timestamp the code uses; 2026-10-28 and
2026-10-29 (which main had stamped) stayed empty. Whether listed createdAt
should prefer ctime when it better reflects Engine install time is a follow-up,
not this PR.

